you've ever seen

00:10:17.501 --> 00:10:20.934
because Russia wouldn't even
need an airplane attack.

00:10:20.934 --> 00:10:23.701
One tank, one shot through that
beautiful glass building

00:10:23.701 --> 00:10:25.000
and it's gone.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.033
Same architect
I used in Chicago.

00:10:27.033 --> 00:10:30.400
Great architects, but they
didn't have war in mind.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.267
But when things happen,
that building would be gone

00:10:32.267 --> 00:10:33.968
in about 15 minutes.

00:10:33.968 --> 00:10:37.501
They should have spent
a $500 million bunker.

00:10:37.501 --> 00:10:41.367
Nice, thick ceiling, six inches,
six feet of concrete.

00:10:41.367 --> 00:10:43.300
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.133 --> 00:10:49.067
Sure, but it's the left
that has a mind virus.

00:10:49.067 --> 00:10:53.467
This -- this is like watching
an HGTV home makeover show

00:10:53.467 --> 00:10:56.567
where the host has
a massive head wound.

00:10:56.567 --> 00:10:59.501
"Okay, I like the subway tile
you have here in the kitchen.

00:10:59.501 --> 00:11:01.367
But I'm thinking instead
of a breakfast nook,

00:11:01.367 --> 00:11:02.501
what you could really use here

00:11:02.501 --> 00:11:04.234
is a steel reinforced
concrete bunker

00:11:04.234 --> 00:11:07.400
in case Russia decides
to nuke your house.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.934
Also, barn doors are so 2009."

00:11:10.934 --> 00:11:13.133
-As addled as Trump
was when he was in office,

00:11:13.133 --> 00:11:14.667
he's an even
more scatterbrained now.

00:11:14.667 --> 00:11:16.667
That's what you get
when you move to a golf resort

00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:18.300
in Florida,
where the sun fries your brain

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.000
and you're surrounded by
other old weirdos or waitstaff

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.634
who are required to tell you
all your ideas are awesome.

00:11:24.634 --> 00:11:26.968
"So that's why NATO
should build a beautiful bunker

00:11:26.968 --> 00:11:29.734
using the same architects
I used in Chicago in case Russia

00:11:29.734 --> 00:11:31.334
decides to bomb them
with a tank.

00:11:31.334 --> 00:11:32.567
What do you think?"

00:11:32.567 --> 00:11:33.801
"That sounds great, Mr. Trump.

00:11:33.801 --> 00:11:36.834
Now, would you like
ketchup with your omelet?"

00:11:36.834 --> 00:11:38.434
"You know I'm trying to cut down
on my cholesterol,

00:11:38.434 --> 00:11:42.267
so skip the omelet and just give
me a big ol' plate of ketchup."

00:11:42.267 --> 00:11:45.534
But at some point, Trump got to
what I assume was supposed to be

00:11:45.534 --> 00:11:48.234
the central premise
of his 2024 campaign

00:11:48.234 --> 00:11:49.934
with this startling line

00:11:49.934 --> 00:11:52.667
about how he could finally
complete the assault

00:11:52.667 --> 00:11:54.667
on democracy he began in 2020.

00:11:54.667 --> 00:11:57.267
-And if you put me back
in the White House,

00:11:57.267 --> 00:11:59.200
their reign is over there.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.767
Their reign will be over,
and they know it.

00:12:01.767 --> 00:12:04.267
And America will be
a free nation once again.

00:12:04.267 --> 00:12:06.133
We're not a free nation
right now.

00:12:06.133 --> 00:12:09.601
We don't have free press.
We don't have free anything.

00:12:09.601 --> 00:12:14.033
In 2016, I declared
I am your voice.

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:18.634
Today I add, I am your warrior,
I am your justice.

00:12:18.634 --> 00:12:22.434
And for those who have been
wronged and betrayed,

00:12:22.434 --> 00:12:23.834
I am your retribution.

00:12:23.901 --> 00:12:25.801
I am your retribution.

00:12:25.801 --> 00:12:27.767
-He was such a terrible
president, and now

00:12:27.767 --> 00:12:29.267
he's auditioning to be Batman.

00:12:29.267 --> 00:12:31.601
But problem -- problem is

00:12:31.601 --> 00:12:32.901
he would never respond
to the bat signal

00:12:32.901 --> 00:12:34.567
because there's no way
he's ever just looking

00:12:34.567 --> 00:12:35.901
pensively out the window.

00:12:35.901 --> 00:12:38.133
You'd have to text it to him
or just shine it on

00:12:38.133 --> 00:12:39.334
Sean Hannity's forehead.

00:12:39.334 --> 00:12:41.167
Oh, you know what you can do?

00:12:41.167 --> 00:12:43.033
You can project it
on a solar eclipse.

00:12:43.033 --> 00:12:45.033
He looks at those.

00:12:45.033 --> 00:12:47.200
Also, that line is
so much less dramatic

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.767
when Trump says it in that soft
singsong voice he uses.

00:12:50.767 --> 00:12:53.834
Like, when Batman says stuff
like that, at least he growls.

00:12:53.834 --> 00:12:56.601
Trump sounds like he's humming
a song he heard on the radio.

00:12:56.601 --> 00:12:58.100
"♪ I am your warrior ♪

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:02.300
♪ I am --
I am your retribution ♪

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.200
♪ You can count on me ♪

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.901
♪ My name is Tiny D ♪

00:13:06.901 --> 00:13:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:13:08.634 --> 00:13:11.067
Even though DeSantis
wasn't at CPAC,

00:13:11.067 --> 00:13:12.067
he made it clear that his

00:13:12.067 --> 00:13:13.467
priorities are very much
the same.

00:13:13.467 --> 00:13:15.601
The modern conservative movement
doesn't have answers

00:13:15.601 --> 00:13:18.067
to the very real problems
facing Americans today.

00:13:18.067 --> 00:13:20.400
So instead, they want
to use government to fix

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.200
all the petty little
cultural grievances they have.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.334
CPAC offered a revealing
and embarrassing glimpse

00:13:25.334 --> 00:13:26.834
into the unhinged modern GOP.

00:13:26.834 --> 00:13:29.734
They have two terrible choices,
a Big D that tanked the party

00:13:29.734 --> 00:13:31.634
in three straight elections
or a Tiny D

00:13:31.634 --> 00:13:32.634
that's no bigger than...

00:13:32.634 --> 00:13:33.801
-Six inches.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:33.801 --> 00:13:36.334
-That has been
"A Closer Look."

00:13:36.334 --> 00:13:40.234
♪♪

